==Hindi==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|hi}} {{term|द्व|tr=dvá|sc=Deva}} (or a closely related Old-Indo-Aryan language, through a Prakrit intermediate), from {{etyl|iir-pro|hi}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|hi}} {{recons|dwóh₁|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Numeral===
{{cardinalbox|hi|1|2|3|एक|तीन|ord=दूसरा|wplink=}}
'''दो''' (do)

# {{cardinal|lang=hi}} [[two]] (2)
#: Number in Devanāgarī script: (२)
#: Number in Arabic script: (٢)
#: Roman numeral: (II)

===Verb===
'''दो''' (do)

# [[give]], the second person singular, [[तुम]] (informal) level [[imperative]] of verb [[देना]]
#: "मुझे पैसे दो" - "[Please] give me money", or literally "To me money give".
#:: Can be softened with a compound use of [[देना]] to: "मुझे पैसे दे दो"

